1
00:00:30,600 --> 00:02:42,099
Ready?
准备好了吗？

2
00:02:42,149 --> 00:03:57,270
Go.
开始吧。

3
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,579
Welcome to the stage,
欢迎登上舞台，

4
00:03:58,629 --> 00:04:10,550
NVIDIA founder and CEO, Jensen Huang.
英伟达创始人兼首席执行官黄仁勋。

5
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,910
Hello, Las Vegas.
大家好，拉斯维加斯。

6
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,189
Happy New Year.
新年快乐。

7
00:04:16,239 --> 00:04:18,950
Welcome to CES.
欢迎参加CES。

8
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,030
Well, we have about 15 keynotes worth of material to pack in here.
嗯，我们这儿得塞进大约15场主题演讲的内容。

9
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:25,246
I'm so happy to see all of you.
我非常高兴见到大家。

10
00:04:25,296 --> 00:04:27,128
You got 3,000 people in this auditorium.
这个礼堂里有3000人。

11
00:04:27,178 --> 00:04:29,914
There's 2,000 people in the courtyard watching us.
广场上有2000人在观看我们。

12
00:04:29,964 --> 00:04:35,329
There's another thousand people apparently in the fourth floor where there were supposed to be NVIDIA show floors,
据说还有1000人在四楼，那里本该是英伟达的展区，

13
00:04:35,379 --> 00:04:42,910
all watching this keynote, and of course, millions around the world are going to be watching this to kick off this new year.
所有正在观看这场主题演讲的人，当然，全球数百万观众也将通过这场演讲迎接新的一年。

14
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:48,950
Well, every 10 to 15 years, the computer industry resets.
每隔10到15年，计算机产业就会迎来一次重置。

15
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,590
A new platform shift happens.
一次新的平台转型正在发生。

16
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:57,910
From mainframe to PC, PC to internet, internet to cloud, cloud to mobile.
从大型机到个人电脑，从个人电脑到互联网，从互联网到云，从云到移动设备。

17
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:03,682
Each time, the world of applications target a new platform.
每一次，应用领域都会转向新的平台。

18
00:05:03,732 --> 00:05:05,649
That's why it's called a platform shift.
这就是为什么它被称为平台转型。

19
00:05:05,699 --> 00:05:09,910
You write new applications for a new computer.
你为新的计算机编写新的应用。

20
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:18,750
Except this time, there are two simultaneous platform shifts in fact happening at the same time.
但这一次，实际上正同时发生两次平台转型。

21
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:25,310
While we now move to AI, applications are now going to be built on top of AI.
当我们转向AI时，应用将建立在AI之上。

22
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:34,070
At first, people thought AIs are applications, and in fact, AIs are applications, but you're going to build applications on top of AIs.
最初人们认为AI就是应用，而实际上AI确实是应用，但你将基于AI构建新的应用。

23
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:44,110
But, in addition to that, how you run the software, how you develop the software fundamentally changed.
此外，软件的运行方式和开发方式也从根本上发生了改变。

24
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:49,590
The entire five-layer stack of the computer industry is being reinvented.
计算机产业的整个五层架构正在被重新发明。

25
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:54,430
You no longer program the software, you train the software.
你不再编写软件，而是训练软件。

26
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:58,870
You don't run it on CPUs, you run it on GPUs.
你不再在 CPU 上运行它，而是在 GPU 上运行。

27
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:06,670
And whereas applications were pre-recorded, pre-compiled, and run on your device,
以往的应用程序是预先录制、预先编译并在你的设备上运行的，

28
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:17,070
now applications understand the context and generate every single pixel, every single token, completely from scratch every single time.
现在的应用程序能够理解上下文，并每次从零开始生成每一个像素、每一个词元。

29
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:23,732
Computing has been fundamentally reshaped as result of accelerated computing, as result of artificial intelligence.
由于加速计算和人工智能的推动，计算方式已从根本上被重塑。

30
00:06:23,782 --> 00:06:29,470
Every single layer of that five-layer cake is now being reinvented.
那个五层蛋糕的每一层如今都在被重新发明。

31
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:39,386
Well, what that means is some 10 trillion dollars or so of the last decade of computing is now being modernized to this new way of doing computing.
换句话说，过去十年约一万亿美金的计算投入，如今正被现代化为这种新的计算方式。

32
00:06:39,436 --> 00:06:46,099
What that means is hundreds of billions of dollars, a couple hundred billion dollars in VC funding each year,
这意味着每年数百亿甚至数百亿美元的风险投资资金，

33
00:06:46,149 --> 00:06:49,506
is going into modernizing and inventing this new world.
正投入于这一新世界的现代化与创新。

34
00:06:49,556 --> 00:07:00,030
And what it means is a hundred trillion dollars of industry, several percent of which is R&D budget, is shifting over to artificial intelligence.
这意味着数百万亿美元的产业，其中数个百分点的研发预算，正转向人工智能。

35
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:02,232
People ask, "Where is the money coming from?"
人们问：“钱从哪里来？”

36
00:07:02,282 --> 00:07:04,790
That's where the money is coming from.
钱就来自这里。

37
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:13,689
The modernization of AI to AI, the shifting of R&D budgets from classical methods to now artificial intelligence methods.
人工智能的现代化，研发预算从传统方法转向人工智能方法的转变。

38
00:07:13,739 --> 00:07:19,286
Enormous amounts of investments coming into this industry, which explains why we're so busy.
大量投资涌入这一行业，这解释了我们为何如此忙碌。

39
00:07:19,336 --> 00:07:21,790
And this last year was no difference.
去年的情况也毫无例外。

40
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,350
This last year was incredible.
去年简直令人难以置信。

41
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:28,350
This last year, there's a slide coming.
去年，有一项关键进展正在浮现。

42
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:30,870
This is what happens when you don't practice.
这就是不练习的后果。

43
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:34,870
2025 was an incredible year.
2025 年是极其非凡的一年。

44
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:39,990
It's just see It seems like everything was happening all at the same time, and in fact, it probably was.
似乎所有事情都在同一时间发生，事实上很可能确实如此。

45
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:43,910
The first thing, of course, is scaling laws.
首先，当然是缩放定律。

46
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:51,819
In 20 15, the first language model that I thought was really going to make a difference made a huge difference.
2015 年，我第一次认为真正能带来改变的语言模型带来了巨大影响。

47
00:07:51,869 --> 00:07:53,093
It was called BERT.
它叫做 BERT。

48
00:07:53,143 --> 00:07:56,190
2017, transformers came.
2017 年，Transformer 模型问世。

49
00:07:56,240 --> 00:08:06,030
It wasn't until 5 years later, 2022, that ChatGPT moment happened, and it awakened the world to the possibilities of artificial intelligence.
直到五年后的2022年，ChatGPT时刻才真正到来，它让全世界意识到人工智能的可能性。

50
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:10,510
Something very important happened a year after that.
那之后一年，发生了一件非常重要的事。

51
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:16,310
The first 01 model from ChatGPT, the first reasoning model, completely revolutionary,
ChatGPT推出的首个01模型，首个具备推理能力的模型，完全革命性的突破，

52
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:21,842
invented this idea called test time scaling, which is very common sense common sensical thing.
首次提出了“测试时扩展”这一概念，这其实是一个非常合乎常理的想法。

53
00:08:21,892 --> 00:08:29,430
Not only do we pre-train a model to learn, we post-train it with our reinforcement learning so that it could learn skills.
我们不仅对模型进行预训练以学习知识，还通过强化学习进行后训练，使其掌握技能。

54
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:33,750
And now we also have test time scaling, which is another way of saying thinking.
现在我们还拥有了测试时扩展，这本质上就是“思考”的另一种说法。

55
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:35,429
You think in real time.
你在实时地进行思考。

56
00:08:35,479 --> 00:08:41,109
Each one of these phases of artificial intelligence requires enormous amount of compute.
人工智能发展的每一个阶段都需要巨大的算力支持。

57
00:08:41,159 --> 00:08:43,011
And the computing law continued to scale.
而计算能力的提升仍在持续扩展。

58
00:08:43,061 --> 00:08:46,190
Large language models continued to get better.
大型语言模型持续变得更好。

59
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,376
Meanwhile, another breakthrough happened.
与此同时，另一项突破也发生了。

60
00:08:48,426 --> 00:08:52,270
And this breakthrough happened in 2024.
这项突破发生在2024年。

61
00:08:52,320 --> 00:09:00,310
Agentic systems starting to emerge, and 2025, it started to pervade to to proliferate just about everywhere.
代理式系统开始涌现，到了2025年，它们开始无处不在地扩散。

62
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:08,750
Agentic models that have the ability to reason, look up information, do research, use tools,
代理式模型具备推理、查找信息、开展研究、使用工具的能力，

63
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:15,144
plan futures, simulate outcomes, all of a sudden started to solve very, very important problems.
规划未来、模拟结果，突然间开始解决非常非常重要的问题。

64
00:09:15,194 --> 00:09:22,667
One of my favorite agentic models is called Cursor, which revolutionized the way we do software programming at NVIDIA.
我最喜欢的代理式模型之一叫Cursor，它彻底改变了英伟达进行软件编程的方式。

65
00:09:22,717 --> 00:09:26,590
Agentic systems are going to really take off from here.
代理式系统将真正开始腾飞。

66
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:28,510
Of course, there were other types of AI.
当然，还有其他类型的AI。

67
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:31,676
We know that large language models isn't the only type of information.
我们知道，大型语言模型并不是唯一的信息形式。

68
00:09:31,726 --> 00:09:39,450
Wherever the universe has information, wherever the universe has structure, we could teach a large language model,
无论宇宙中何处存在信息，无论何处存在结构，我们都可以训练一个大型语言模型，

69
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:48,028
a form of language model, to go understand that information, to understand its representation, and to turn that into an AI.
一种语言模型形式，去理解这些信息，理解其表达方式，并将其转化为AI。

70
00:09:48,078 --> 00:09:55,630
One of the biggest, most important one is physical AI, AIs that understand the laws of nature.
其中最大、最重要的一种是物理AI，即理解自然法则的AI。

71
00:09:55,680 --> 00:10:00,510
And then, of course, physical AIs is about AIs interacting with the world.
而物理AI则关乎AI与世界的互动。

72
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:06,062
But, the world itself has information encoded information, and that's called AI physics.
但世界本身也编码了信息，这种信息被称为AI物理。

73
00:10:06,112 --> 00:10:11,270
AI that in the case of physical AI, you have AI that interacts with the physical world,
人工智能在物理人工智能的情况下，是指与物理世界交互的人工智能，

74
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:16,025
and you have AI physics, AI that understands the laws of physics.
以及人工智能物理学，即理解物理定律的人工智能。

75
00:10:16,075 --> 00:10:23,110
And then, lastly, one of the most important things that happened last year, the advancement of open models.
最后，去年最重要的事情之一，是开源模型的发展。

76
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:30,043
We can now know that AI is going to proliferate everywhere when open source, when open innovation,
现在我们可以确定，当开源、开放创新成为可能时，

77
00:10:30,093 --> 00:10:35,933
when innovation across every single company and every industry around the world is activated at the same time.
当全球每一个公司和每一个行业同时被激活创新时，人工智能将无处不在。

78
00:10:35,983 --> 00:10:39,502
Open models really took off last year.
去年，开源模型真正开始腾飞。

79
00:10:39,552 --> 00:10:50,670
In fact, last year, we saw the advance of DeepSeek R1, the first open model that's a reasoning system.
事实上，去年我们见证了 DeepSeek R1 的进步，这是首个具备推理能力的开源模型。

80
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:57,922
It caught the world by surprise, and it activated literally this entire movement.
它令世界感到震惊，并真正激活了整个运动。

81
00:10:57,972 --> 00:10:59,799
Really, really exciting work.
真的非常令人激动的工作。

82
00:10:59,849 --> 00:11:01,350
We're so happy with it.
我们对此感到无比欣喜。

83
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:10,718
Now, we have openings open model systems all over the world of all different kinds, and we now know that open models have also reached the frontier.
如今，全球各地出现了各种各样的开源模型系统，我们如今也清楚，开源模型已经达到了前沿水平。

84
00:11:10,768 --> 00:11:14,789
Still solidly is 6 months behind the frontier models,
仍然比前沿模型落后约六个月。

85
00:11:14,839 --> 00:11:22,070
but every single 6 months a new model is emerging, and these models are getting smarter and smarter.
但每隔六个月就会出现一个新模型，这些模型变得越来越聪明。

86
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:27,789
Because of that, you could see the number of downloads has exploded.
正因为如此，你可以看到下载量已经爆炸式增长。

87
00:11:27,839 --> 00:11:34,258
The number of downloads is growing so fast because startups want to participate in the AI revolution,
下载量增长如此迅速，是因为初创公司想要参与人工智能革命，

88
00:11:34,308 --> 00:11:40,550
large companies want to, researchers want to, students want to, just about every single country wants to.
大公司想要，研究人员想要，学生想要，几乎每个国家都想要。

89
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:46,700
How is it possible that intelligence, the digital form of intelligence, will leave anyone behind?
人工智能，这种数字化形式的智能，怎么可能让任何人落后呢？

90
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:52,544
And so, open models has really revolutionized artificial intelligence last year.
因此，开放模型去年真正革新了人工智能。

91
00:11:52,594 --> 00:11:56,105
This entire industry is going to be reshaped as a result of that.
由于这一变化，整个行业都将被重塑。

92
00:11:56,155 --> 00:11:59,190
Now, we had this inkling some time ago.
现在，我们早些时候就已有所察觉。

93
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:05,755
You might have heard that several years ago, we just started to build and operate our own AI supercomputers.
你可能听说过，几年前我们就开始自行构建和运营自己的AI超级计算机。

94
00:12:05,805 --> 00:12:07,739
We call them DGX Clouds.
我们称它们为DGX云。

95
00:12:07,789 --> 00:12:11,959
A lot of people asked, "Are you going to going into the cloud business?"
很多人问：“你们会进入云业务吗？”

96
00:12:12,009 --> 00:12:16,419
The answer is no. We're building these DGX supercomputers for our own use.
答案是否定的。我们建造这些DGX超级计算机是供自己使用的。

97
00:12:16,469 --> 00:12:24,654
Well, it turns out we have billions of dollars of supercomputers in operation, so that we could develop our open models.
事实上，我们已有数十亿美元的超级计算机在运行，这使我们能够开发开源模型。

98
00:12:24,704 --> 00:12:28,110
I am so pleased with the work that we're doing.
我对我们正在做的工作感到非常高兴。

99
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:31,685
It is starting to attract attention all over the world and all over the industries,
它正开始吸引全球各地、各行各业的关注，

100
00:12:31,735 --> 00:12:37,670
because we are doing frontier AI model work in so many different domains.
因为我们正在众多不同领域开展前沿人工智能模型的研究。

101
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:44,030
The work that we did in proteins, in digital biology, La Proteina, to be able to synthesize and generate proteins.
我们在蛋白质、数字生物学、La Proteina 方面的工作，能够合成和生成蛋白质。

102
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:49,550
OpenFold 3 to understand the understand the structure of proteins.
OpenFold 3 用于理解蛋白质的结构。

103
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:59,623
Evo 2, how to understand and generate multiple proteins, otherwise the beginnings of cellular cellular representation.
Evo 2 用于理解并生成多种蛋白质，这正是细胞表征的开端。

104
00:12:59,673 --> 00:13:02,907
Earth 2, AI that understands the laws of physics.
Earth 2，一种理解物理定律的人工智能。

105
00:13:02,957 --> 00:13:10,990
The work that we did with FourCastNet, the work that we did with CorrDiff, really revolutionized the way that people are doing weather prediction.
我们与 FourCastNet 和 CorrDiff 的合作工作，真正革新了人们进行天气预测的方式。

106
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:15,077
NeMo-Megatron, we've now doing groundbreaking work there.
在 NeMo-Megatron 方面，我们如今正开展开创性的工作。

107
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:23,142
The first hybrid transformer SSM model that's incredibly fast and therefore can think for a very long time,
这是首个混合的变换器 SSM 模型，速度极快，因此能长时间思考，

108
00:13:23,192 --> 00:13:29,780
or can think very quickly with that for not a very long time, and produce very very smart intelligent answers.
或在短时间内快速思考，并生成极其智能、精准的答案。

109
00:13:29,830 --> 00:13:36,830
NeMo-Megatron 3 is groundbreaking work, and you can expect us to deliver other versions of NeMo-Megatron 3 in the near future.
NeMo-Megatron 3 是开创性的工作，未来不久您将看到我们推出 NeMo-Megatron 3 的其他版本。

110
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:45,750
Cosmos, a frontier open world foundation model, one that understand how the world works.
Cosmos 是一个前沿的开放世界基础模型，能够理解世界运作的原理。

111
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:52,546
GR00T, a humanoid robotic system, articulation, mobility, locomotion, these models,
GR00T 是一个人形机器人系统，涵盖关节、移动性和运动控制，这些模型，

112
00:13:52,596 --> 00:13:59,056
these technologies are now being integrated, and in the each one of these cases open to the world.
这些技术现在正被整合，且在每种情况下都对世界开放。

113
00:13:59,106 --> 00:14:01,767
Frontier humanoid robotics models open to the world.
前沿人形机器人模型对世界开放。

114
00:14:01,817 --> 00:14:07,397
And then, today, we're going to talk a little bit about Alpamayo, the work that we've been doing in self-driving cars.
今天，我们将简要谈谈 Alpamayo，以及我们在自动驾驶汽车方面所开展的工作。

115
00:14:07,447 --> 00:14:15,550
Not only do we open source the models, we also open source the data that we used to train those models.
我们不仅开源模型，还开源了用于训练这些模型的数据。

116
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:22,270
Because that in that way, only in that way can you truly trust how the models came to be.
因为只有通过这种方式，您才能真正信任这些模型是如何诞生的。

117
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,892
We open source all the models.
我们开源了所有模型。

118
00:14:23,942 --> 00:14:26,006
We help you make derivatives from them.
我们帮助您基于这些模型衍生出新的成果。

119
00:14:26,056 --> 00:14:27,932
We have a whole suite of libraries.
我们提供了一整套工具库。

120
00:14:27,982 --> 00:14:34,002
We call them NeMo libraries, physics NeMo libraries, and the Clara NeMo libraries, each bio NeMo libraries.
我们将它们称为 NeMo 工具库、物理 NeMo 工具库和 Clara NeMo 工具库，以及各个生物 NeMo 工具库。

121
00:14:34,052 --> 00:14:41,049
Each one of these libraries are life cycle management systems of AIs, so that you could process the data, you could generate data,
这些库都是AI的生命周期管理系统，让你能够处理数据、生成数据，

122
