I um their their entire AI and data processing platform is being integrated and accelerated by NVIDIA today.
我们目前正将他们的整个AI和数据处理平台集成并加速，由英伟达实现。

254
00:25:38,560 --> 00:25:44,142
ServiceNow, the world's leading customer service and um employee service platform.
ServiceNow，全球领先的客户服务和员工服务平合。

255
00:25:44,192 --> 00:25:48,594
Snowflake, the world's top data platform in the cloud.
Snowflake，全球领先的云数据平台。

256
00:25:48,644 --> 00:25:51,688
Uh incredible work that that uh is being done there.
那里正在进行的工作令人难以置信。

257
00:25:51,738 --> 00:25:52,726
Uh Code Rabbit.
代码兔子。

258
00:25:52,776 --> 00:25:55,336
Uh we're using Code Rabbit all over NVIDIA.
我们在英伟达的各个地方都在使用代码兔子。

259
00:25:55,386 --> 00:26:00,662
Uh CrowdStrike creating AIs to detect, define AI threats.
CrowdStrike正在创建AI，用于检测和定义AI威胁。

260
00:26:00,712 --> 00:26:10,270
Uh NetApp, their AI their data platform now has NVIDIA semantic AI on top of it and agentic systems on top of it for them to do customer service.
NetApp，他们的AI数据平台现在已搭载英伟达语义AI，并在其之上构建了代理式系统，用于客户服务。

261
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:18,915
But the important thing is this, not only is this the way that you develop applications now, this is going to be the user interface of your platform.
重要的是，这不仅是当前开发应用的方式，更将成为你平台的用户界面。

262
00:26:18,965 --> 00:26:29,230
So whether it's Palantir or ServiceNow or Snowflake and many other companies that we're working with, the agentic system is the interface.
无论是Palantir、ServiceNow、Snowflake，还是我们正在合作的众多其他公司，代理式系统就是接口。

263
00:26:29,280 --> 00:26:35,042
It's no longer Excel with a bunch of, you know, squares that you enter enter information into.
它不再是Excel那种一堆你输入信息的方格。

264
00:26:35,092 --> 00:26:38,120
Maybe it's no longer could just command line.
也许它也不再仅仅是命令行。

265
00:26:38,170 --> 00:26:47,184
The any all of that multimodality information is now possible and the way you interact with your platform is much more well,
现在，多模态信息的任意组合已成为可能，你与平台的交互方式也变得更加自然流畅，

266
00:26:47,234 --> 00:26:50,430
if you will, simple, like you're interacting with people.
用你的话说，就像在与人互动一样简单。

267
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:55,771
And so that's enterprise AI being revolutionized by agentic systems.
因此，代理式系统正在彻底革新企业级 AI。

268
00:26:55,821 --> 00:26:57,804
The next thing is physical AI.
下一个方向是物理 AI。

269
00:26:57,854 --> 00:27:00,864
This is an area that you've seen me talk about for several years.
这是我多年来一直谈论的一个领域。

270
00:27:00,914 --> 00:27:03,670
In fact, we've been working on this for eight years.
事实上，我们已经在这个方向上深耕了八年。

271
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:04,762
The question is,
问题在于，

272
00:27:04,812 --> 00:27:10,555
how do you take something that is intelligent inside a computer and interacts
如何将计算机内部的智能体，从仅通过屏幕和扬声器与你交互，

273
00:27:10,605 --> 00:27:17,047
with you with screens and speakers to something that can interact with the world,
转变为能够与现实世界互动的实体，

274
00:27:17,097 --> 00:27:22,070
meaning it can understand the common sense of how the world works.
意味着它能理解世界运作的常识。

275
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:23,039
Object permanence.
物体恒存性。

276
00:27:23,089 --> 00:27:27,110
If I look away and I look back, that object is still there.
即使我转过头离开，再回头，那个物体依然存在。

277
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,059
Um causality.
但因果关系。

278
00:27:28,109 --> 00:27:29,882
If I push it, it tips over.
如果我推它，它就会倒下。

279
00:27:29,932 --> 00:27:32,240
It understands friction and gravity.
它理解摩擦力和重力。

280
00:27:32,290 --> 00:27:34,400
It understands inertia.
它理解惯性。

281
00:27:34,450 --> 00:27:39,969
That a heavy truck rolling down the road is going to need a little bit more time to stop.
一辆重型卡车在道路上行驶时，需要更多时间才能停下。

282
00:27:40,019 --> 00:27:43,629
That a ball is going to keep on rolling.
一个球会持续滚动下去。

283
00:27:43,679 --> 00:27:49,925
These ideas are common sense to even a little child, but for AI, it's completely unknown.
这些概念对一个小孩来说都是常识，但对人工智能而言却完全陌生。

284
00:27:49,975 --> 00:27:57,228
And so we have to create a system that allows AIs to learn the the common sense of the physical world,
因此我们必须创建一个系统，让人工智能能够学习物理世界的常识，

285
00:27:57,278 --> 00:28:02,987
learn its laws, but also to be able to, of course,
学习其规律，同时也能够，

286
00:28:03,037 --> 00:28:13,072
learn from data and the data is quite scarce, and to be able to evaluate whether that AI is working, meaning it has to simulate in an environment.
从数据中学习，而数据却相当稀少，还必须能够评估该人工智能是否在正常工作，这意味着它必须在环境中进行模拟。

287
00:28:13,122 --> 00:28:18,945
How does an AI know that the the actions that it's performing is consistent with what it should
人工智能如何知道它所执行的动作与应有的行为一致？

288
00:28:18,995 --> 00:28:24,455
do if it doesn't have the ability to simulate the response of the physical world back on its actions?
如果它不具备模拟物理世界对其动作反应的能力，又如何得知？

289
00:28:24,505 --> 00:28:31,070
The response of its actions is really important to simulate, otherwise there's no way to evaluate it, it's different every time.
其行为的响应对于模拟至关重要，否则就无法评估，每次的结果都不同。

290
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:35,990
And so this basic system requires three computers.
因此这个基础系统需要三台计算机。

291
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:41,869
One computer, of course, the one that we know that NVIDIA builds for training the AI models.
一台计算机，当然是我们所知的英伟达用于训练AI模型的那台。

292
00:28:41,919 --> 00:28:46,422
Another computer that we know is to inference the compute inference the models.
另一台计算机，我们所知的是用于推理的计算推理模型。

293
00:28:46,472 --> 00:28:55,390
Inferencing the model is essentially a robotics computer that runs in the car or runs in a robot or runs in a factory, runs anywhere at the edge.
推理模型本质上是一台机器人计算机，可在汽车、机器人或工厂中运行，也可在任何边缘位置运行。

294
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:59,114
But there has to be another computer that's designed for simulation.
但必须还有一台专为模拟设计的计算机。

295
00:28:59,164 --> 00:29:03,046
And simulation is at the heart of almost everything NVIDIA does.
模拟几乎贯穿了英伟达所做的所有工作。

296
00:29:03,096 --> 00:29:06,550
This is This is where we are most comfortable.
这正是我们最擅长的领域。

297
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:12,079
And simulation was really the foundations of almost everything that we've done with physical AI.
模拟确实是我们在物理AI方面所做一切的基础。

298
00:29:12,129 --> 00:29:18,758
So we have three computers and multiple stacks that run on these computers, these libraries to make them useful.
因此我们有三台计算机，以及运行在这些计算机上的多个软件栈，这些库使它们变得有用。

299
00:29:18,808 --> 00:29:24,190
Omniverse is our digital twin physically based simulation world.
Omniverse 是我们的数字孪生物理基础模拟世界。

300
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:32,590
Cosmos, as I mentioned earlier, is our foundation model, not a foundation model for language, but a foundation model of the world.
正如我之前提到的，Cosmos 是我们的基础模型，不是语言的基础模型，而是世界的基座模型。

301
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:35,310
And it's also aligned with language.
而且它也与语言对齐。

302
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:37,977
You could say something like, you know, what's happening to the ball?
你可以说类似这样的话，你知道，球正在发生什么？

303
00:29:38,027 --> 00:29:40,588
And they'll tell you the ball's rolling down the street.
他们会告诉你球正在沿着街道滚动。

304
00:29:40,638 --> 00:29:44,665
And so a world foundation model and then, of course, the robotics models.
然后是一个世界基础模型，当然还有机器人模型。

305
00:29:44,715 --> 00:29:46,017
We have two of them.
我们有两个。

306
00:29:46,067 --> 00:29:48,390
One of them is called GR00T.
其中一个叫 GR00T。

307
00:29:48,440 --> 00:29:51,230
The other one's called Alpamayo that I'm going to tell you about.
另一个叫 Alpamayo，我接下来会跟你们讲到。

308
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:57,555
Now, the one of the most important things that we have to do with physical AI is to create the data to train the AI in the first place.
我们在物理 AI 上必须做的最重要的一件事，就是创建用于训练 AI 的数据。

309
00:29:57,605 --> 00:29:59,710
Where does that data come from?
这些数据从哪里来？

310
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:09,550
Rather than instead of having languages because we created a bunch of text that are what we consider ground truth that the AI can learn from,
不是像我们创建大量文本那样，那些文本是我们认为的真实情况，AI 可以从中学习，

311
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:12,276
how do we teach an AI the ground truth of physics?
我们该如何教 AI 真实的物理规律？

312
00:30:12,326 --> 00:30:21,430
There are lots and lots of videos, lots and lots of videos, but hardly enough to capture the diversity and the type of interactions that we need.
虽然有大量视频，大量视频，但几乎不足以捕捉我们所需的多样性和交互类型。

313
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:31,870
And so, this is where great minds came together and transformed what used to be compute into data.
于是，这里就是伟大思想汇聚之地，将原本的计算转变为数据。

314
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:38,981
Now, using synthetic data generation that is grounded and conditioned by the laws of physics,
现在，利用基于物理定律生成的合成数据，

315
00:30:39,031 --> 00:30:49,542
grounded and conditioned by ground truth, we can now selectively cleverly generate data that we can then use to train the AI.
基于真实数据进行约束和引导，我们可以有选择地、巧妙地生成数据，进而用于训练人工智能。

316
00:30:49,592 --> 00:31:01,190
So, for example, what comes into this AI, this Cosmos AI world model on the left on over here, is the output of a traffic simulator.
举个例子，输入到左侧这个宇宙AI世界模型中的，是交通模拟器的输出结果。

317
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:06,630
Now, this traffic simulator is hardly enough for an AI to learn from.
然而，仅靠这个交通模拟器，人工智能很难从中学习。

318
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:11,390
We can take this, put it into a Cosmos Foundation model,
我们可以将这些数据输入到宇宙基础模型中，

319
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:19,898
and generate surround video that is physically based and physically plausible that the AI can now learn from.
生成基于物理、符合物理规律的环绕视频，让人工智能能够从中学习。

320
00:31:19,948 --> 00:31:22,072
And there are so many examples of this.
这样的例子还有很多。

321
00:31:22,122 --> 00:31:28,110
Let me show you what Cosmos can do.
让我来展示一下宇宙模型的能力。

322
00:31:28,160 --> 00:31:32,750
The Chat GPT moment for physical AI is nearly here.
物理AI的ChatGPT时刻即将来临。

323
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:34,416
But the challenge is clear.
但挑战显而易见。

324
00:31:34,466 --> 00:31:39,070
The physical world is diverse and unpredictable.
物理世界是多样且不可预测的。

325
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:45,110
Collecting real-world training data is slow and costly, and it's never enough.
收集真实世界的训练数据既缓慢又昂贵，而且永远都不够。

326
00:31:45,160 --> 00:31:48,550
The answer is synthetic data.
答案是合成数据。

327
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:56,710
It starts with NVIDIA Cosmos, an open frontier world foundation model for physical AI.
它始于英伟达 Cosmos，一个面向物理 AI 的开放前沿世界基础模型。

328
00:31:56,760 --> 00:32:04,790
Pre-trained on internet-scale video, real driving and robotics data, and 3D simulation.
基于互联网规模的视频、真实驾驶和机器人数据，以及 3D 模拟进行预训练。

329
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:13,830
Cosmos learned a unified representation of the world, able to align language, images, 3D, and action.
Cosmos 学习了世界的统一表示，能够对齐语言、图像、3D 和动作。

330
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:21,150
It performs physical AI skills like generation, reasoning, and trajectory prediction.
它能执行物理 AI 技能，如生成、推理和轨迹预测。

331
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:27,350
From a single image, Cosmos generates realistic video.
仅凭一张图像，Cosmos 就能生成逼真的视频。

332
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:33,590
From 3D scene descriptions, physically coherent motion.
根据 3D 场景描述，生成物理上一致的运动。

333
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:39,710
From driving telemetry and sensor logs, surround video.
根据驾驶遥测数据和传感器日志，生成环绕视频。

334
00:32:39,760 --> 00:32:45,350
From planning simulators, multi-camera environments.
根据规划模拟器，生成多相机环境。

335
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:51,150
Or from scenario prompts, it brings edge cases to life.
或者根据场景提示，让边缘案例栩栩如生。

336
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:55,870
Developers can run interactive closed-loop simulations in Cosmos.
开发者可以在 Cosmos 中运行交互式的闭环模拟。

337
00:32:55,920 --> 00:33:00,910
When actions are made, the world responds.
当采取行动时，世界会作出回应。

338
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:03,510
Cosmos reasons.
宇宙模型进行推理。

339
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:13,790
It analyzes edge scenarios, breaks them down into familiar physical interactions, and reasons about what could happen next.
它分析边缘场景，将其分解为熟悉的物理交互，并推理接下来可能发生的情况。

340
00:33:13,840 --> 00:33:19,270
Cosmos turns compute into data, training AVs for the long tail,
宇宙模型将算力转化为数据，用于训练自动驾驶汽车应对长尾场景，

341
00:33:19,320 --> 00:33:30,990
and robots how to adapt for every scenario.
以及让机器人学会适应各种情境。

342
00:33:31,040 --> 00:33:33,990
I know, it's incredible.
我知道，这太不可思议了。

343
00:33:34,040 --> 00:33:39,246
Cosmos is the world's leading foundation model, world foundation model.
宇宙模型是全球领先的通用基础模型。

344
00:33:39,296 --> 00:33:43,390
It's been downloaded millions of times, used all over the world.
它已被下载数百万次，全球各地都在使用。

345
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:47,321
Getting world getting the world ready for this new era of physical AI.
正在让世界为这个物理 AI 的新时代做好准备。

346
00:33:47,371 --> 00:33:49,670
We use it ourselves as well.
我们自己也在使用它。

347
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:54,990
We use it ourselves to create our self-driving car.
我们用它来打造自己的自动驾驶汽车。

348
00:33:55,040 --> 00:34:00,230
Using it for scenario generation and using it for evaluation,
用于场景生成，也用于评估。

349
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:10,109
we could have something that allows us to effectively travel billions, trillions of miles, but doing it inside a computer.
我们可以拥有某种技术，让我们在计算机内部实现数十亿、数万亿英里的有效旅行。

350
00:34:10,159 --> 00:34:12,199
And we've made enormous progress.
我们已经取得了巨大的进展。

351
00:34:12,249 --> 00:34:23,710
Today, we're announcing Alpamayo, the world's first thinking, reasoning autonomous vehicle AI.
今天，我们宣布推出Alpamayo，这是世界上首个具备思考与推理能力的自动驾驶AI。

352
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:31,030
Alpamayo is trained end to end, literally from camera in to actuation out.
Alpamayo采用端到端训练，真正实现了从摄像头输入到执行输出的完整流程。

353
00:34:31,080 --> 00:34:37,430
The camera in, lots and lots of miles that are driven by itself using human demonstration,
摄像头输入的数据，来自它自身通过人类示范驾驶的大量里程。

354
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:41,550
and we have lots and lots of miles that are generated by Cosmos.
此外，我们还通过宇宙系统生成了海量的里程数据。

355
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:50,536
In addition to that, hundreds of thousands of examples are labeled very, very carefully so that we could teach the car how to drive.
除此之外，还有数十万条经过极其精细标注的样本，用于教会汽车如何驾驶。

356
00:34:50,586 --> 00:34:53,910
Alpamayo does something that's really special.
Alpamayo做了一件非常特别的事。

357
00:34:53,960 --> 00:35:00,417
Not only does it take sensor input and activates steering wheel, brakes,
它不仅接收传感器输入并控制方向盘、刹车和油门，

358
00:35:00,467 --> 00:35:07,696
and and acceleration, it also reasons about what action it's about to take.
还会推理自己即将采取的动作。

359
00:35:07,746 --> 00:35:15,830
It tells you what action it's going to take, the reasons by which it came about that action, and then of course the trajectory.
它会告诉你它将采取什么动作，做出该决定的原因，以及相应的行驶轨迹。

360
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:27,230
All of these are coupled directly and trained very specifically by a large combination of human trained and as well as Cosmos generated data.
所有这些都直接耦合，并通过大量人类训练数据与宇宙系统生成数据的组合，进行了专门训练。

361
00:35:27,280 --> 00:35:29,951
The result of it is just really incredible.
结果令人惊叹不已。

362
00:35:30,001 --> 00:35:38,590
Not only does your car drive as you would expect it to drive, and it drives so naturally because it learned directly from human demonstrators,
你的汽车不仅像你预期的那样行驶，而且行驶得如此自然，因为它直接从人类示范者那里学到了驾驶方式。

363
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:42,869
but in every single scenario when it comes up to the scenario, it reasons about it,
但在每一个场景中，它都会对此进行推理，

364
00:35:42,919 --> 00:35:46,790
tells you what it's going to do, and it reasons about what it's what it's about to do.
